# Packaged plugin distribution artifacts (the marketplace reads source files
# directly — committing the bundled .plugin archive at the repo root makes
# the marketplace API treat it as a packaged plugin source and fail
# extraction due to the duplicate .claude-plugin/ structure inside).
*.plugin
*.zip

# Python bytecode. This repo ships one bundled helper script, and importing it
# locally creates a __pycache__ alongside it. A .pyc embeds the source
# docstring, so an uncommitted-by-accident one also trips the PII scan.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# macOS
.DS_Store
